      <node id="Robotics" label="Robotics">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="concept" />
          <attvalue for="5" value="The field involving the design, construction, operation, and use of robots." />
          <attvalue for="3" value="Engineering" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="2025-03-06 23:54:43.573929" />
          <attvalue for="7" value="['persona_24', 'persona_70', 'persona_4']" />
          <attvalue for="8" value="[{'description': 'Both robotics and music theory emphasize the importance of mastering rules to enable creative exploration.', 'evidence': &quot;It's about knowing the rules so well that you can bend them without breaking them.&quot;, 'novelty_score': 0.7, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574103', 'source_conversation': ['persona_24', 'persona_70', 'persona_4']}, {'description': 'The concept of a robotics orchestra playing jazz highlights the potential for creative collaboration between robotics and music.', 'evidence': &quot;Maybe one day, we'll have a robotics orchestra. Robots playing jazz—now that would be something to see!&quot;, 'novelty_score': 0.9, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574128', 'source_conversation': ['persona_24', 'persona_70', 'persona_4']}]" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="Music Theory" label="Music Theory">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="concept" />
          <attvalue for="5" value="The study of the practices and possibilities of music." />
          <attvalue for="3" value="Music" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="2025-03-06 23:54:43.573942" />
          <attvalue for="7" value="['persona_24', 'persona_70', 'persona_4']" />
          <attvalue for="8" value="[{'description': 'The intersection of technology and music has been present since the 1950s with computerized music.', 'evidence': 'By the way, did you know that some of the earliest computerized music was actually made on mainframes back in the 1950s?', 'novelty_score': 0.8, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574089', 'source_conversation': ['persona_24', 'persona_70', 'persona_4']}, {'description': 'Both robotics and music theory emphasize the importance of mastering rules to enable creative exploration.', 'evidence': &quot;It's about knowing the rules so well that you can bend them without breaking them.&quot;, 'novelty_score': 0.7, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574115', 'source_conversation': ['persona_24', 'persona_70', 'persona_4']}, {'description': 'The concept of a robotics orchestra playing jazz highlights the potential for creative collaboration between robotics and music.', 'evidence': &quot;Maybe one day, we'll have a robotics orchestra. Robots playing jazz—now that would be something to see!&quot;, 'novelty_score': 0.9, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574140', 'source_conversation': ['persona_24', 'persona_70', 'persona_4']}, {'description': 'Music and sports both benefit from technology, but still rely on human guidance for emotional and expressive elements.', 'evidence': 'Technology can provide tools and resources, but the human element is important for interpreting those tools and offering guidance.', 'novelty_score': 0.8, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574515', 'source_conversation': ['persona_4', 'persona_70']}, {'description': 'Learning music might improve athletic performance by enhancing rhythm and timing.', 'evidence': 'Rhythm is a big part of basketball too. You’ve got to have great timing and coordination.', 'novelty_score': 0.7, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574543', 'source_conversation': ['persona_4', 'persona_70']}, {'description': &quot;Both music and sports involve moments of realization where understanding clicks, similar to a 'light bulb moment'.&quot;, 'evidence': &quot;I often tell my students that once they understand the theory, the music will start to make more sense to them in ways they never expected. It's like a light bulb moment for them.&quot;, 'novelty_score': 0.6, 'timestamp': '2025-03-06 23:54:43.574562', 'source_conversation': ['persona_4', 'persona_70']}]" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
